# English repository text

Text that is stored in this repo or published on GitHub is English. Replies in chat follow the user's language.

## Commits and GitHub

- Commit subjects and bodies are English, imperative, and say why.
- Pull request titles and descriptions, issue titles and bodies, release notes, and labels are English.
- Do not mix Chinese into any of that text.

```
fix: keep the sent line on the card

The kernel is not connected yet, so the line has nowhere else to go.
```

## Comments and docs

- Code comments, doc comments, and TODOs are English.
- README and other docs checked into the repo are English.
- Do not add a Chinese comment, even a short one.

```ts
// The kernel is not connected yet; keep the line on this card.
```

User-facing UI copy may stay Chinese. That is product language, not a comment or a commit.
